+# Fix: `eraseOnClick` doesn't work as expected (upstream issue #322)
+
+## Problem
+Clicking on an empty square or a piece of the other color always erases all drawn
+shapes (`drawClear` in `src/drag.ts` `start()`), regardless of any config. The only
+knob, `drawable.eraseOnMovablePieceClick`, only guards clicks on a (unselected)
+piece of the turn color. There is no way to disable erase-on-click entirely.
+
+## Plan
+- [x] 1. Reproduce: add `tests/draw.test.ts` with headless `drag.start` clicks
+      (empty square / opponent piece / own piece) asserting shapes survive when
+      `drawable.eraseOnClick: false`. 4 tests failed before the fix.
+- [x] 2. Fix: reintroduce `drawable.eraseOnClick` (default `true`) as the master
+      switch in `src/draw.ts` (`Drawable`), `src/state.ts` (`defaults`),
+      `src/config.ts` (config docs), and gate `drawClear` in `src/drag.ts`.
+      Semantics:
+      - `eraseOnClick: false` -> clicking never clears shapes.
+      - `eraseOnClick: true`  -> clicking an empty square or immovable piece
+        clears; clicking a movable piece clears only when
+        `eraseOnMovablePieceClick` is true (current behavior preserved).
+- [x] 3. Run `npm test` -> all green (11/11: 3 pre-existing + 8 new).
+- [x] 4. Typecheck (`npx tsc --noEmit`) clean; lint (`npm run lint`) clean;
+      oxfmt-clean (verified against HEAD with LF-normalized copies; the local
+      `check-format` noise is CRLF from `core.autocrlf=true`, pre-existing).
+
+## Review
+**Root cause** - `drag.start()` called `drawClear()` whenever
+`(eraseOnMovablePieceClick || !piece || piece.color !== s.turnColor)`, so the
+`!piece` / other-color branches always erased all shapes and no config could
+disable erase-on-click. The historical master switch `eraseOnClick` had been
+renamed to `eraseOnMovablePieceClick` with narrower semantics; the fix from
+upstream PR #176 (which the issue asks for) was never merged.
+
+**Fix** - `drawable.eraseOnClick` (default `true`) is now the master switch in
+`drag.start()`: when `false`, clicking never clears shapes; when `true`, the
+previous per-square behavior applies (incl. `eraseOnMovablePieceClick`).
+Default behavior is unchanged.
+
+**Files changed**
+- `src/drag.ts` - gate `drawClear(s)` on `s.drawable.eraseOnClick`
+- `src/draw.ts` - `Drawable.eraseOnClick` field
+- `src/state.ts` - default `eraseOnClick: true`
+- `src/config.ts` - public `drawable.eraseOnClick` option + doc comments
+- `tests/draw.test.ts` - new: 8 regression tests (headless `drag.start` clicks)
+
+**Verification**
+- Before fix: 4 of the 8 new tests fail (shapes erased despite
+  `eraseOnClick: false`); the 4 default-behavior tests pass, proving the harness
+  reproduces current behavior.
+- After fix: `npm test` 11/11 green; `tsc --noEmit` and `oxlint` clean.
